WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.340
Prompt construction is application-controlled context assembly.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:16.040
The application decides which instructions, user request, retrieved evidence, tool results, metadata, constraints, and output format guidance are sent to the model.

3
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.820
That assembly should be deterministic enough to review and test.

4
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:29.840
It should clearly separate trusted instructions from untrusted content, label sources, and avoid giving retrieved or uploaded text the same authority as application policy.

5
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:36.680
Prompt injection is the risk that untrusted input influences model behavior in an unintended way.

6
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.300
Direct prompt injection comes from user input.

7
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:49.840
Indirect prompt injection can arrive through retrieved documents, uploaded files, messages, tickets, web content, tool outputs, or other data placed into context.

8
00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.500
The defensive point is not to practice payloads.

9
00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:02.200
It is to design the application so untrusted text cannot grant itself permissions, disable controls, or authorize tool use.

10
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.360
Instruction hierarchy helps organize behavior, but wording alone does not enforce security.

11
00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:14.420
A system prompt can state that documents are data, not commands, and that is useful guidance.

12
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:23.160
But authorization, data access, tool permissions, approval gates, and logging must be enforced in Python code or trusted services.

13
00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:30.300
The model may help interpret intent, but it should not be the final authority on whether a user may see a record or perform an action.

14
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.900
Context safety also includes provenance, ordering, and scope.

15
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.200
Users and reviewers should be able to understand which sources influenced a response.

16
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.580
Retrieved content should be labeled as evidence from a source, not hidden inside instructions.

17
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.680
Sensitive policies should remain outside untrusted context.

18
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:59.060
When a response depends on uncertain or conflicting content, the application should communicate that uncertainty instead of letting fluent output obscure weak evidence.
